      "reason": null,
      "answer": "The spray booth face-velocity gauge can look fine while real airflow is too low due to calibration drift producing a falsely-high reading rather than an actual airflow problem. Verify true face velocity with an independent handheld anemometer at several points across the booth opening; if true readings are below 0.5 m/s despite an acceptable gauge reading, stop spraying and schedule gauge recalibration immediately.",
